From: lumia930-linux
Subject: [PATCH] target: msm8974: remove framebuffer relocation hack

applies against Mainline4Lumia/lk2nd, branch martini-support
(https://github.com/Mainline4Lumia/lk2nd/tree/martini-support)

the branch's target_init() points the mdp scanout register at
0x0ff00000, which is uninitialized ram, so the display shows
noise for the rest of the lk session (no text is drawn there).
combined with 0001's raised kernel load address, the two would
also collide: the forced kernel address 0x10008000 sits inside
the 1080x1920x4 framebuffer that would start at 0x0ff00000.

removing the relocation leaves scanout on the live uefi
framebuffer at 0x00400000 (the address bootshim's own display
output already uses), so bootshim's text stays visible and
nothing overlaps the raised kernel address range.
---
--- a/target/msm8974/init.c
+++ b/target/msm8974/init.c
@@ -366,19 +366,10 @@
 #endif


-#define FB_ADDR_REG             0xFD901E14
-#define FB_NEW_ADDR             0x0FF00000
-
 void target_init(void)
 {
 	dprintf(INFO, "target_init()\n");

-	dprintf(INFO, "relocating framebuffer to 0x%d", FB_NEW_ADDR);
-	writel(FB_NEW_ADDR, FB_ADDR_REG);
-	writel(0x1, 0xfd900618);
-	writel(0x1, 0xfd900718);
-
-
 	spmi_init(PMIC_ARB_CHANNEL_NUM, PMIC_ARB_OWNER_ID);

 	/* Save PM8941 version info. */
